ate their importance by going on strike ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d01", "start": 341, "end": 518, "text": "Image source , Women 's History Archives Instead of going to the office , doing housework or childcare they took to the streets in their thousands to rally for equal rights with"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d02", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "disambiguation ) ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d02", "start": 19, "end": 314, "text": "1975 Icelandic women 's strike Women 's Day Off Date 24 October 1975 Location Iceland Caused by Gender pay gap , occupational sexism Goals To `` demonstrate the indispensable work of women for Iceland 's economy and society '' and `` protest wage discrepancy and unfair employment practices '' ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d02", "start": 315, "end": 568, "text": "Methods Women 's strike On 24 October 1975 , Icelandic women went on strike for the day to `` demonstrate the indispensable work of women for Iceland 's economy and society '' [ 1 ] and to `` protest wage discrepancy and unfair employment practices '' ."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d03", "start": 0, "end": 185, "text": "2018 Spanish women's strike On March 8, 2018, International Women's Day, Spanish women went on strike for the day to denounce sexual discrimination, domestic violence and the wage gap ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d03", "start": 186, "end": 430, "text": "Participants, led by women's organizations and the trade unions, did not go to their paid jobs, especially in education, and did not do any housework or child-rearing for the whole day; some groups additionally called for a consumption strike ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d03", "start": 431, "end": 585, "text": "The unions estimate that 5 million women participated in the strike, with massive demonstrations taking place in the most populated cities of the country."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d03", "start": 586, "end": 612, "text": "The action was part of the"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04", "start": 0, "end": 204, "text": "War, about 50,000 women brought together by Women Strike for Peace marched in 60 cities in the United States to demonstrate against nuclear weapons under the slogan \"End the Arms Race not the Human Race\"."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04", "start": 205, "end": 275, "text": "It was the largest national women's peace protest of the 20th century."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04", "start": 276, "end": 386, "text": "About 1,500 women led by Dagmar Wilson gathered at the foot of the Washington Monument while President John F."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04", "start": 387, "end": 436, "text": "Kennedy watched from a window at the White House."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04", "start": 437, "end": 557, "text": "The protest helped \"push the United States and the Soviet Union into signing a nuclear test-ban treaty two years later\"."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04", "start": 558, "end": 589, "text": "In January 1962, Berkeley Women"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "24 October 1975", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d00:c0", "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d01:c0", "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d02:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "March 8, 2018", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d03:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "1961", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9:d04:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0404-ff7df3fcbbb9